## Prerequisites

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for Python package management
- [AWS CDK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/) for infrastructure deployment
- [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) for local development and production builds
- SSH access to the `co-cddo` GitHub organisation

## Getting started

1. Open the project in VS Code and reopen in the dev container when prompted.

2. Provide AWS credentials to the dev container:

   ```bash
   idea-app provide-role
   ```

3. The dev container serves the app at <http://localhost:8080> with
   auto-reload. For Streamlit, Dash and FastAPI apps it is started by the
   "Run app" VS Code task (allow automatic tasks if VS Code asks). If your code
   has an error, the traceback appears in that terminal and the container keeps
   running. See `.devcontainer/README.md` for details.

4. Check the production image builds and passes its health check:

   ```bash
   idea-app smoke-test
   ```

## Deployment

This project uses AWS CDK for infrastructure. See `app.py` for the stack definition.

## Testing

```bash
uv run pytest
```

